# There is already a meta-layer we can reuse too

The project **Dstack Private AI Gateway** is particularly useful.

It's an open-source OpenAI-compatible gateway that can verify/reroute multiple confidential inference providers, including:

```text
Tinfoil
NEAR AI
Chutes
Secret AI
Phala direct
generic ACI providers
```

and produces signed receipts/attestation information. ([GitHub][19])

That may mean we don't even need to build much of our own TEE-router verification logic.

Potentially:

```text
                 STEALTH
                    │
              ModelRouter
                    │
          Private AI Gateway
             /       |       \
            /        |        \
        Phala     Chutes     Tinfoil
          │          │          │
        TEE        TEE        TEE
```

That is exactly consistent with our “don't rebuild shit” rule.

