## Most interesting setup right now

For **your specific app**, my initial stack would be:

```text
STEALTH
  │
  ├─ Goose
  │
  ├─ model router
  │    │
  │    ├─ Chutes
  │    │     cheap TEE
  │    │
  │    ├─ Phala / RedPill
  │    │     TEE + uncensored
  │    │
  │    ├─ Venice
  │    │     uncensored + TEE/E2EE
  │    │
  │    └─ local model
  │          highest privacy
  │
  ├─ SimpleX
  ├─ Monero
  ├─ XMRBazaar
  └─ Tor
```

And I'd make **attestation an actual runtime condition**, not a badge:

```text
sensitive request
      ↓
request fresh attestation
      ↓
verify
      ↓
PASS ──→ send prompt
FAIL ──→ do not transmit
```

That's exactly the sort of thing QP is good for.

The biggest discovery here is that we **don't need to choose between “uncensored” and “TEE” anymore**. There are already practical APIs giving us both, especially **Phala/RedPill and Venice**, while **Chutes** gives us an extremely cheap confidential default pool.

